1. Properly implements the data method according to the docstring requirements
2. Handles both index and key-based access to record data
3. Returns a dictionary with requested keys and their values
4. Sets None for keys that don't exist in the record
5. Raises IndexError for out-of-bounds indexes
6. Assumes self has keys() and values() methods as part of the RecordExporter class
7. Handles the case when no keys are provided by returning all key-value pairs

The code now properly returns a dictionary instead of None, which resolves the AttributeError mentioned in the feedback.

