<repaired_code>
def find_roots(
    graph: "Graph", prop: "URIRef", roots: Optional[Set["Node"]] = None
) -> Set["Node"]:
    """Find the roots in some sort of transitive hierarchy."""
    # Get all subjects that have the given property
    subjects = set(graph.subjects(prop))
    
    # Get all objects that are used with the given property
    objects = set(graph.objects(prop))
    
    # Roots are subjects that never appear as objects
    # (i.e., they have no parents in the hierarchy)
    roots_set = subjects - objects
    
    # If specific roots are provided, intersect with found roots
    if roots is not None:
        roots_set &= roots
        
    return roots_set
</repaired_code>

The fixed code:
1. Gets all subjects that have the specified property
2. Gets all objects that are used with the specified property
3. Finds roots by identifying subjects that never appear as objects (meaning they have no parents)
4. If specific roots are provided, intersects them with the found roots
5. Returns the final set of root nodes

This implementation follows the docstring requirements by finding nodes that are at the top of the hierarchy (have no parents) for the given property, such as RDFS.subClassOf.

